 ],
 "notes": "Two-part layout: a full-width header band (helmet-with-blue-plume icon, gold small-caps title, six tabs, red close button) above an open book (leather cover, left and right parchment pages split by a dark gutter at x 661-667). Tabs: All is SELECTED (warm gold-brown fill, bright gold frame with diamond studs top/bottom centre and corner flourishes, gold book icon and gold label); Enemies/Bosses/Units/Spells/Relics are unselected (dark slate fill, thin brass frame, grey-white icons and labels) and abut each other with a shared brass divider. Left page: 'DISCOVERED' heading, a flourish rule, 'PAGE 1 OF 7' and prev/next chevron buttons (both drawn identically, so prev is not visibly disabled on page 1), then a 3x3 grid of portrait cells (column pitch 160, gutters ~11 px; row 1 is 136 tall, rows 2-3 are 132 tall in the concept). Each cell is a dark well in a thin brass frame with corner rivets and the same crossed-quill emblem top-left (cell.N.corner). Cell 1 (Shield Knight) is SELECTED: glowing orange-gold frame with outer bloom and a warm-brown well. Cells 2-7 are discovered (full-colour figures). Cells 8 and 9 are LOCKED: a dark smoky silhouette with a grey '?' (recorded as text cell.8.lock / cell.9.lock). A small flourish ornament sits centred under the grid. Right page shows the selected entry: bold dark serif name, a role chip (dark shield badge with gold shield icon + tan ribbon with swallowtail end, 'Frontline'), a one-line blurb, a large portrait well with ragged painted vignette edges (no frame; the rect is the median edge, the figure's helmet nearly touches the top), two dark stat tiles with brass frames and corner rivets (heart/HEALTH 108, sword/DAMAGE 12; caption small grey caps, value large cream serif), a snowflake-and-line divider, a 4-line lore paragraph, and a slate BACK TO MAP button with a brass frame and scroll icon (label left-aligned after the icon, not centred). A faint sepia caravan sketch decorates the top-right of the right page (background art, not interactive). Banners and lanterns outside the book are backdrop. Fit caveats: concept lettering is narrower/taller than Cinzel/Crimson, so sizes are width-fitted and glyphs render slightly shorter; lore line 2 is ~9 px tighter in the concept than Crimson 500/14 (kept the paragraph's common size); stat values fit 24 ('108') vs 28 ('12') because the concept digits are condensed, so use one size (~26) for both in practice. The selected 'All' label fits size 17 against 15 for the other tab labels (it is drawn slightly larger in the concept)."
}